    ontouml:description """Female Sex is refined into distinct characterizations that capture the basis used for determining female sex. Karyotypic Female Sex, Phenotypic Female Sex, and Sex-at-birth Female Sex provide karyotypic, phenotypic, and birth-record perspectives while keeping Female Sex as the shared reference category.

Female-sex Person is specialized into corresponding person categories that track the same basis of determination. The links between each person category and its corresponding female sex category keep the classification basis explicit across karyotypic, phenotypic, and sex-at-birth perspectives.""" ;
    ontouml:name "Female Sex"@en ;
    ontouml:owner :3zRjNDmD.AAAARX7 ;
    ontouml:project :qmUW4emAUygeIwWe .

