    ontouml:description """Sex is the general entry point for sex classification and is refined into Phenotypic Sex and Karyotypic Sex, with Sex at Birth positioned as a specialization of Phenotypic Sex to represent a recorded classification at birth.

The basic sex categories Male Sex, Female Sex, and Indeterminate Sex provide anchors that are further specialized into modality-specific counterparts, including phenotypic, karyotypic, and sex-at-birth variants, with Phenotypic Ambiguous Sex aligned with indeterminacy in the phenotypic modality.""" ;
    ontouml:name "Sex Overview"@en ;
    ontouml:owner :29MUuemGAqAEHBDu ;
    ontouml:project :qmUW4emAUygeIwWe .

