    ontouml:description """Self-identified Gender frames the classification of a self-aware person in terms of the gender with which that person identifies. It establishes self-identification as the basis for relating a person's gender classification to that person's own awareness and identification.

Self-identified Gender is differentiated into male, female, and non-binary cases, with corresponding person classifications for self-identified male-gender, female-gender, and non-binary-gender persons. The non-binary branch is further refined into agender and two-gender person cases, preserving the distinction between broader non-binary identification and these more specific forms.""" ;
    ontouml:name "Self-identified Gender"@en ;
    ontouml:owner :XGQUIDmGAqAEHCgG ;
    ontouml:project :qmUW4emAUygeIwWe .

