    ontouml:description """Gender is organized as a taxonomy that distinguishes a general notion of gender from several attribution modalities that reflect how gender is expressed, identified, or recorded. The taxonomy separates personal identification from external attribution and from institutionally recorded forms, supporting explicit distinctions between self-identified, externally-attributed, administrative, and legal variants of gender.

Within each attribution modality, gender categories are specialized into male, female, and non-binary forms, enabling consistent classification across different sources of gender information. Gender expression is represented as a related branch with its own categories, allowing expression-oriented classification to be used alongside attribution-oriented classification while keeping these perspectives conceptually distinct.""" ;
    ontouml:name "Gender Taxonomy"@en ;
    ontouml:owner :DMmUuemGAqAEHBFZ ;
    ontouml:project :qmUW4emAUygeIwWe .

