:67OOsemAUygeIx3n a ontouml:Class ;
    ontouml:description "A Person with Variant Sex Chromosome is represented as an individual whose chromosomal composition departs from the most common XX or XY configurations. In the model this class complements the regular category, ensuring that cases of chromosomal variation are consistently represented. It specializes Person and accounts for less frequent patterns, maintaining completeness and disjointness with the regular classification to capture chromosomal diversity in a systematic way (reflected in Variant Karyotypical Female Person and Variant Karyotypical Male Person)." ;
    ontouml:isAbstract false ;
    ontouml:isDerived false ;
    ontouml:isExtensional false ;
    ontouml:isPowertype false ;
    ontouml:name "Person with Variant Sex Chromosome"@en ;
