    ontouml:description "Phenotypic Ambiguous Sex denotes the classification of a person's phenotypic sex as ambiguous when observable sex characteristics do not clearly align with male-typical or female-typical patterns in an assessment context. It provides an explicit representation of ambiguity at the level of phenotypic observation, distinct from chromosome-based classification and from administrative recording at birth." ;
